{
"esm": "1.3.0",
"metadata": {
 "name": "cam_vertical_diffusion",
 "description": "CAM6 vertical diffusion (dump site vdiff) as a PDE on the EarthSciDiscretizations column grid (stage 2 of the EqESM project): the implicit Euler-backward finite-volume solve of vertical_diffusion_solver.F90 / diffusion_solver.F90 (components/cam/src/atmos_phys/schemes/vertical_diffusion/ of the instrumented cam6_4_212 fork) written as du/dt = d/dz(K du/dz) + tau_damp u + src_u, with the layer field u (zonal wind; v, s, q mirrored) on lev (1 = surface) and the interface coefficient K = interface_diffusivity(kv, dpidz_sq) on lev_nodes. The surface-layer sources src_u/v/s/q and the wind damping are the cam_templates laws surface_layer_source (the pver injection g F / dz[1], diffusion_solver.F90:440, 491-499 for the residual stress, 779 for shflx, 974-975 and 1056-1061 for cflx with the dryfac conversion) and wind_damping_rate (tau_damp = -g ksrf / dz[1] at pver, 0 elsewhere, F90:274-285) with the drag coefficient ksrf = surface_stress_coefficient(taux, tauy, u0, v0, ksrftms) = ksrftms + max(tau/ws, ksrfmin) (F90:232-239; wsmin/ksrfmin are the module parameters F90:42-44). The sources are explicit sources rather than the flux rule's boundary condition because the CLI cannot express them as the BC: the rule's prescribed-flux free names kdudz_bot/kdudz_top cannot be renamed at the import edge (rename reaches only exports; the names are free inside the rule body) and are shared across every firing, so one units-typed declaration carries one value and one unit class, while the four fields' fluxes differ in both (verified: import-rename of kdudz_bot fails with template_import_rename_unknown_name). The diffusion term is lowered by EarthSciDiscretizations' varcoeff_face_laplacian_lev_flux_bc (interface-valued coefficient, no face averaging, layer-centre gradient spacing, prescribed fluxes at both domain faces) -- exactly the CAM finite-volume stencil of linear_1d_operators.F90 (spr/sub/diag, deriv_diag): with the CAM solve's default BoundaryFixedFlux conditions at both ends the prescribed face fluxes are the free names kdudz_bot/kdudz_top, and in this dump window they are zero (taux = tauy = shflux = 0 with CLUBB_SGS, vertical_diffusion.F90:1017-1035, and kvh(1) = 0, dse_top = 0), so the two names are declared units-free after the ysu.esm idiom and shared by all four equations (a units-typed declaration could satisfy only one field). The coordinate is the CAM interface pressure with the sign flipped: ze = -pint reversed, so ze increases upward and esd lev i <-> CAM lev 33-i; dz[i] = pdel(33-i), z_top = ze[NLEV+1], and the interface flux rule's zc/dz come from the grid templates applied to ze. The residual-stress memory is tauresx = tauresx_enter - tauimpx with tauimpx = integral((u-u0)/(g dt), lev, z_sfc, z_top) (diffusion_solver.F90:536-589, taux = tautmsx = taubljx = 0 in the window), the integral lowered by integral_lev_whole over the measure dz; tauimpy mirrors v. ramda = dt/timeres (F90:491-496, am_correction = .false., timeres = 7200 s). The kinetic-energy dissipation dtk = 0.5(u0^2+v0^2) - 0.5(u^2+v^2) enters the s equation as dtk/dt (F90:598-646 do_beljaars branch). Tracer diffusion is a generic q equation with the explicit surface source (the q solve's explicit flux-to-state conversion q1(pver) += dt g cflx / pdel, F90:974-975; the pdel/pdeldry conversion for dry constituents appears as the dryfac parameter, F90:1056-1061). Tests pin the dump rows of cam_vdiff_prof.csv / cam_vdiff_q.csv (steps 1, 2, 48; the site runs with do_iss = do_beljaars = itaures = .true., am_correction = .false., and all kvh/kvm/kvq = 0, so the dumped tendencies are the tau_damp, taures-source and dtk laws only); the nonzero-K operator row is a compiled-Fortran reference (stage1/analysis/cam_vdiff_driver/, linear_1d_operators.F90 verbatim with the CAM gfortran build's -DUSE_CONTIGUOUS=, default fixed-flux boundaries) applying A to the step-1 u0 at K = dpidz_sq (kv = 1 m2/s), reversed to esd order. The s-equation top boundary is a documented gap: CAM's dse solve uses BoundaryFixedLayer(0)/BoundaryData(dse_top) at the top (flux 2 K(1) (dse_top - s(1))/del(1), nonzero only when K(1) > 0) while the rule's shared kdudz_top is zero-flux; the window has kvh(1) = 0 and dse_top = 0 so the two coincide here. All parameters and states are in esd order (reversed from the dump rows).",
 "license": "MIT",
 "tags": [
  "stage2",
  "cam",
  "vertical_diffusion",
  "pde",
  "dump-pinned",
  "esd:column_nonuniform_1d",
  "esd:varcoeff_face_laplacian_lev_flux_bc"
  ]
 },
"metaparameters": {
 "NLEV": {
  "type": "integer",
  "default": 32,
  "description": "Number of model layers (CAM pver = 32). Bound into the column grid and rules at the import edges; the model equations spell the top interface as NLEV+1 (the ground upper-bound name z_top of the integral rule, esm-spec 9.6.1)."
  }
 },
"models": {
 "CamVerticalDiffusion": {
  "expression_template_imports": [
   {
    "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
    "only": [
     "column_cell_center",
     "column_cell_thickness"
     ],
    "bindings": {
     "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
   {
    "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/varcoeff_face_laplacian_lev_flux_bc.esm",
    "bindings": {
     "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
   {
    "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/integral_lev_whole.esm",
    "bindings": {
     "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
   {
    "ref": "./cam_templates.esm",
    "only": [
     "interface_diffusivity",
     "surface_layer_source",
     "surface_stress_coefficient",
     "wind_damping_rate"
     ]
    }
   ],
  "variables": {
